An end-to-end test proves that the Ridgeline fixture imports through the full parser → mapper → import service chain under source `ridgeline`, and that a Stratus automation run does not retire Ridgeline stations.

**Scope** — `tests/e2e/fixtures/lookup_sites.json` (add Highmoor sites), `tests/e2e/test_xml_import_pipeline.py` (append). Uses `tests/services/xml_import/fixtures/ridgeline_feed.xml` (M1) and `InMemoryImportedStationRepository(source=…, store=…)` (M2). No production code.

#### Tasks

| Task | Description | Files | SP | Status |
|------|-------------|-------|----|--------|
| 4.1 | Add sites `Brackenridge` (id 204), `Cold Fell` (id 205), `Sainte-Élise` (id 206, names `[{"lang":"fr","name":"Sainte-Élise"}]`) under region key `"31"` (Highmoor) | `tests/e2e/fixtures/lookup_sites.json` | 1 | pending |
| 4.2 | Append `class TestRidgelineFeedPipeline` with an import test and a cross-source stale-isolation test | `tests/e2e/test_xml_import_pipeline.py` | 1 | pending |

#### Definition of Done

##### Task 4.1
- [ ] The three site objects use the same shape as existing entries (`id`, `name`, `names`). Existing e2e tests still pass.

